1
00:00:00,001 --> 00:00:11,990
Welcome to the TransactHub Designer Studio. This is where a payments designer defines, tests and exports payment workflows. It is a design-time tool: it never reads or changes a running payment.

2
00:00:12,598 --> 00:00:24,992
Everything you do is done as a user, in a tenant. The owner tenant holds shared content: the platform and the schemes. Each bank is a tenant of its own. Roles are enforced, and whoever makes a change never approves it.

3
00:00:25,601 --> 00:00:33,409
The catalogue lists every artefact. A name has four parts: a scope, a type, a name, and the major version. Let us search for IBAN.

4
00:00:34,011 --> 00:00:45,296
This is an activity: a block that a workflow calls. Its contract says what it reads, what it writes, and the outcomes it can end with. The page also shows which workflows use it, and the tests that target it.

5
00:00:45,903 --> 00:00:58,873
Here is the corporate payment workflow, a platform workflow. It validates, screens, checks limits, reserves funds and routes the payment. It has a slot called scheme leg, which a scheme fills, and hook points, where a bank adds its own logic.

6
00:00:59,481 --> 00:01:11,747
Every workflow works on one canonical context, modelled on ISO 20022. Fields that hold personal data are flagged. They must never appear in workflow state, logs, tests or samples.

7
00:01:12,355 --> 00:01:20,035
Reason codes come from the ISO external code sets, kept by version. A M zero four, for example, is insufficient funds.

8
00:01:20,637 --> 00:01:33,607
A scheme has a dispatch table, which routes every message. In the wages protection system, a salary file starts an outward corporate payment. The table names the intake map that reads the file, and the leg that fills the slot.

9
00:01:34,217 --> 00:01:41,043
In the workflow designer, the YAML on the left and the canvas on the right edit the same document. The checks run as you type.

10
00:01:41,646 --> 00:01:50,819
A step that talks to a party and waits for an answer calls a composite. The expanded form is what an engine runs: each composite step becomes a block of inner steps.

11
00:01:51,426 --> 00:02:02,839
Everything that is not a workflow has its own editor: rules, rule sets, decision tables, activity contracts, maps, simulators, composites, ports and schemes. Each runs its gates as you edit.

12
00:02:03,445 --> 00:02:12,810
Tests run on a virtual clock, so a wait of days ends at once. This factory test sends a salary file to a simulator that stands in for the wages protection system.

13
00:02:13,414 --> 00:02:22,160
The business trace has one line for each step. The detail shows the steps inside the submit composite: send the file, await the acknowledgement, and read it.

14
00:02:22,766 --> 00:02:30,659
Now a whole payment, end to end, for the example bank. We bind each port to a simulator, choose a salary file, and name the message it is.

15
00:02:45,074 --> 00:02:58,386
The front door reads the file, picks the corporate workflow, and the WPS leg fills its slot. The payment is screened, funds are reserved, the rail is chosen, the file is submitted and acknowledged, and the payment is posted and settled.

16
00:02:58,993 --> 00:03:08,742
The conformance kit holds forty six scenarios, one for each construct of the language. Every engine must reproduce them: the studio, D T F X, and Flowable.

17
00:03:09,347 --> 00:03:20,077
A bank changes values, not logic: which rails it runs, its limits, and the hooks it binds. Each change is a new release of its configuration set, checked against the bounds the scheme allows.

18
00:03:20,684 --> 00:03:31,734
An export is the package an engine runs. Each task queue gets its own worker, which serves only its own tasks. The manifest also lists the change sets that every artefact was published in.

19
00:03:32,339 --> 00:03:40,936
Governance keeps the record. Every save, approval and refusal goes into a hash-chained audit log, and the studio can verify the chain at any time.

20
00:03:41,541 --> 00:03:54,213
The AI assistant drafts a rule, an activity, a script or a simulator. Start from a template, fill in the parts in angle brackets, and add the source text. The draft runs through the same gates, and it never publishes itself.

21
00:03:54,821 --> 00:04:02,821
That is the tour. In the next demo, we build a new scheme and its workflow from scratch, approve it, enable it for a bank, and pay a file end to end.
